  ("Measurement and Statistics: Measures of Central Tendency", "In descriptive statistics, the three primary measures of central tendency are the Mean, Median, and Mode. When a data distribution contains extreme outliers (e.g., one student scored 100 while all others scored below 20), which measure is the most appropriate and resilient?", "The Median (the middle score, unaffected by extreme outliers).", ["The Mean (the arithmetic average, heavily distorted by outliers).", "The Mode.", "The Standard Deviation."]),
