  ("Normal Distribution: Mean, Median, and Mode Relationship", "In a theoretical, perfectly symmetrical Normal Distribution curve, how are the Mean, Median, and Mode positioned?", "The Mean, Median, and Mode are all exactly EQUAL and located at the exact center of the distribution ($Mean = Median = Mode$).", ["The Mean is greater than the Median and Mode.", "The Mode is greater than the Median and Mean.", "The Median is zero while the Mean is 100."]),
  ("Distribution Skewness: Positively Skewed Distribution", "In a 'Positively Skewed' (Right-Skewed) distribution (e.g., a very difficult examination where most students obtained low scores with a few high outliers), how are the central tendencies arranged?", "Mode < Median < Mean (the Mean is pulled to the right toward the high score tail).", ["Mean < Median < Mode (Negatively Skewed).", "Mean = Median = Mode (Symmetrical).", "Median < Mode < Mean."]),
